{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Minnesota Twins  face  the  New  York  Mets  in  the  2006  World  Series.  Assuming  the  two  teams are  evenly  matched  (each  has  a  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd6d26513bbf9d11197035fe648afccd8c5d706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.5$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />  probability  of  winning  any  game)  what  is  the  probability  that the  World  Series  (a  best  of  7  series  of  games which lasts  until  one  team  wins  four  games)  will require  the  full  seven  games  to  determine  a  winner?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7f5919d4d8e3979a5437df522f08b6eaa11e049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }\\frac{1}{16}\\qquad \\text{(B) }\\frac{1}{8}\\qquad \\text{(C) }\\frac{3}{16}\\qquad \\text{(D) }\\frac{1}{4}\\qquad \\text{(E) }\\frac{5}{16}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e46dd26ec03aeed8b0a38b0625ad076aa840ee8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(F) }\\frac{3}{8}\\qquad \\text{(G) }\\frac{5}{32}\\qquad \\text{(H) }\\frac{7}{32}\\qquad \\text{(I) }\\frac{9}{32}\\qquad \\text{(J) }\\frac{3}{64}\\qquad \\text{(K) }\\frac{5}{64}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"462\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db7b2886eabfe3d757c286355883015b7c7f8841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(L) }\\frac{7}{64}\\qquad \\text{(M) }\\frac{1}{2}\\qquad \\text{(N) }\\frac{13}{32}\\qquad \\text{(O) }\\frac{11}{32}\\qquad \\text{(P) }\\text{none of the above}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"495\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order for the World Series to have seven games, each team must win exactly three times.  The last game does not matter.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/35116fa96e5e68e688359cba498c0f9c880a5b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tbinom{6}{3} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"64\" height=\"22\" /> possibilities, and since all of the possibilities involve each team winning three times, the probability of having 7 games in the World Series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3ec3c41a143794ea5023fe58b9788e9f50219f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\cdot \\left( \\frac12 \\right)^6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{5}{16}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"170\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b